## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/error.html
- Summary (EN): The Error node passes its input through unchanged while generating a message, warning, or error for the network. It is useful for flagging parameter values that would produce unusable results.
- Résumé (FR) : Le nœud Error transmet son entrée sans modification et signale un message, un avertissement ou une erreur selon une condition.

- Inputs meaning: ["input#: layer passed through unchanged; the page lists only this input, and output# is the same layer"]

- Key parameters: ["Number of Errors: how many messages, warnings or errors to generate", "Error Message: text shown when the notice is active; if empty, the notice is not reported", "Severity: Message (node info window only), Warning (badge and text, cooking continues), Error (prominent badge, downstream nodes do not cook)", "Report This Error: expression that triggers the notice when non-zero, for example a threshold check on another node's parameter"]

- Caveats: ["Use the Error severity only for problems the network cannot recover from, because it stops downstream cooking", "Inside a digital asset, notices do not reach the user unless the Error node is added to the asset's Message Nodes list in Operator Type Properties"]

